{
  "dom_id": "step-q67814",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "A pump moves $\\frac{9}{10}$ gallons of water in three minutes. Find the unit rate of gallons per minute.",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the unit rate of gallons per minute, we divide the number of gallons, $\\frac{9}{10},$ by the number of minutes, $3$, as follows:   \n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{10}÷3\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10}÷3 & =\\frac{9}{10}÷\\frac{3}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{10}\\times \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\times 1}{10\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 3}{10\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times \\cancel{3}}{10\\times \\cancel{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{3}{10}$ gallons per minute.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
